      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "This is an example of applying Perlin Noise to create dynamic and natural-looking
    changes in a game environment. Perlin Noise is used to adjust the movement or
    shape of objects dynamically, such as making walls or cubes appear to move up
    and down smoothly. \n\nThis adds a layer of realism and unpredictability, enhancing
    the overall gameplay experience. By incorporating Perlin Noise, the environment
    becomes more interactive and engaging, creating a sense of life within the game.
    \n\nThis technique is particularly effective in games that aim for immersive
    and visually appealing designs, such as horror or adventure genres.\n\nHere is
    a flowchart that explains how it works:"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
